{"author":{"id":"5698b6d16d951325374257d86a2e673da0e55970c3d21c0f7c6f49018f24e5bf"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1790947878,"nonce":"iSl/M/zPmVQJd+7DzYu+sOkApcQ=","message":"**Owner's ruling (2026-10-02): the approval grant is declarative. This comment supersedes the body's open question.**\n\n**The decision.** Who may approve Remedies on a ToolServer is stated by the deployment's configuration (Helm values / config file / environment), in the same declarative layer that already forces tuning keys (`internal/identity/domain/declarative.go`). There is no in-app grant or revoke: the grant is **read-only over the API**, and a write is refused the way a declaratively-managed tuning key is. That answers bootstrap: the first grant is written by whoever writes the values file, which is the same authority that deploys oto. It also means one holder cannot mint a second approver (an alt account) in the UI and defeat double approval (ADR 0054 §4).\n\n**Shape.**\n- A grant is `(org, ToolServer name, user email)`. A user holds it only by their email address, so a shadow member (no address, migration 00074) can never hold one.\n- A grant naming an email that matches no user, or a ToolServer that is not configured, grants nothing. The settings screen shows it as such rather than hiding it. It is not a boot error, because a ToolServer is configured in the database, possibly after the deploy.\n- Malformed config (a bad email, an empty ToolServer name, an unknown key) is refused at boot and names the config key, like every other declarative key.\n- The grant is a permission only. It routes nothing, notifies no one and creates no queue (H-1).\n- ADR 0054 §4 is amended to record this.\n\n**Done when.** A grant can be declared per ToolServer; the API and UI show grants read-only, with their config key as origin; an approval by a non-holder is refused with a typed error; changing the config and restarting changes who may approve; tests cover a holder, a non-holder, an unmatched email, a shadow member and malformed config.\n\n**Mode.** AFK.","files":null}]}